#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# robinson_schensted

#% text
# `robinson_schensted(w)`: the insertion and recording tableaux [P, Q] of the word or permutation

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The insertion tableau P is built by row insertion, the recording tableau Q records where each step ended. A word with repeated letters gives a semistandard P.

#% item
# The length of the first row of P is the length of a longest increasing (non-decreasing) subsequence.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
robinson_schensted([3, 1, 4, 2, 5])
#% output
#= [[[1, 2, 5], [3, 4]], [[1, 3, 5], [2, 4]]]

#% cell
robinson_schensted(cycles([[1, 3], [2, 4]]))
#% output
#= [[[1, 2], [3, 4]], [[1, 2], [3, 4]]]

#% cell
robinson_schensted([1, 2, 2, 1])
#% output
#= [[[1, 1, 2], [2]], [[1, 2, 3], [4]]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `inverse_robinson_schensted`, `standard_young_tableaux`
